</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Baselines</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare MBT against a comprehensive set of baselines:
<span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Base Model (Base)</span>, the vanilla Qwen3 model;
<span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Metacognitive Prompting (Prompt)</span>, which utilizes a system prompt to induce metacognitive behaviors without parameter updates;
<span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(3) Rejection Sampling (RS)</span>, a standard self-distillation approach fine-tuned on correct traces from HotpotQA;
<span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(4) Standard GRPO (GRPO)</span>, which directly optimizes the base model using the same reward as MBT; and
<span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(5) Efficiency-oriented Methods</span> including TokenSkip <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xia et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and LIMOPro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, re-implemented specifically for the MHQA context, strictly adhering to the design details provided in their respective original publications.
Detailed configurations for all baselines are provided in the Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Experimental Details ‣ Mirroring the Mind: Distilling Human-LikeMetacognitive Strategies into Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation Details</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experiments are conducted across the Qwen3 family <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
To ensure a strictly fair comparison, all methods within each scale share identical training configurations (including learning rate, batch size, and epochs) and sampling parameters.
For inference, we use a sampling temperature of 0.6 and top-p of 0.95, mirroring the setup used in DeepSeek-R1 evaluation.
For the teacher model, we employ gpt-oss-120b with the reasoning effort set to high.
To facilitate reproducibility, we have publicly released our code and dataset, including metacognitively grounded training samples at <a href="https://github.com/12kimih/metacognitive-behavioral-tuning" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/12kimih/metacognitive-behavioral-tuning</a></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To strictly assess the impact of MBT on reasoning performance, efficiency, and structural stability, we employ a comprehensive set of metrics covering reasoning accuracy, efficiency, and behavioral stability.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Performance and Efficiency</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For accuracy, we report Exact Match (EM), F1 score, and LLM-as-a-Judge evaluation using gpt-oss-120b. For efficiency, we measure:</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Average Output Length (Len):</span> A proxy for inference-time computational cost.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Degeneration Failures (Degen):</span> The count of outputs exceeding the maximum context limit (32,768 tokens). These cases indicate reasoning collapse, typically caused by the model entering infinite repetitive loops.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
