<td id="S4.T2.5.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.65pt;padding-bottom:0.65pt;"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.10.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">758</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:0.65pt;padding-bottom:0.65pt;"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.10.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_ulem_uline" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">2.71</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.10.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.65pt;padding-bottom:0.65pt;"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">1</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.10.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.65pt;padding-bottom:0.65pt;"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.10.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_ulem_uline" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">743</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.10.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:0.65pt;padding-bottom:0.65pt;"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.10.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_ulem_uline" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">1.18</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.10.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.65pt;padding-bottom:0.65pt;"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.10.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_ulem_uline" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">1</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.10.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.65pt;padding-bottom:0.65pt;"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.10.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_ulem_uline" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">739</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.5.1.10.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.65pt;padding-bottom:0.65pt;"><span id="S4.T2.5.1.10.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_ulem_uline" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2F2F2;">0.78</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Accuracy-Efficiency Score (AES)</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To capture the trade-off between improving accuracy and reducing computational cost in a single scalar, we adopt the Accuracy-Efficiency Score (AES) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
Let <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\text{Length}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Length</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\text{Length}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\text{Acc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Acc</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\text{Acc}</annotation></semantics></math> be the relative changes in length and accuracy compared to the baseline.
AES is calculated as:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{AES}=\begin{cases}\alpha\cdot\Delta\text{Length}+\beta\cdot|\Delta\text{Acc}|,&amp;\text{if }\Delta\text{Acc}\geq 0\\
\alpha\cdot\Delta\text{Length}-\gamma\cdot|\Delta\text{Acc}|,&amp;\text{if }\Delta\text{Acc}&lt;0\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>AES</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Length</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Acc</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Acc</mtext></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Length</mtext></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Acc</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>Acc</mtext></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{AES}=\begin{cases}\alpha\cdot\Delta\text{Length}+\beta\cdot|\Delta\text{Acc}|,&amp;\text{if }\Delta\text{Acc}\geq 0\\
\alpha\cdot\Delta\text{Length}-\gamma\cdot|\Delta\text{Acc}|,&amp;\text{if }\Delta\text{Acc}&lt;0\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As in prior work, we set <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1,\beta=3,\gamma=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1,\beta=3,\gamma=5</annotation></semantics></math> to penalize accuracy degradation more heavily than efficiency gains.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Structural Stability and Behavioral Quality</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify the quality of the reasoning process itself, we employ three specialized metrics using an LLM-as-a-Judge.</p>
<ul id="S4.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overthinking Score (<math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{\text{OT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">OT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{\text{OT}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> measures post-solution stagnation (e.g., redundant verification or baseless doubt) on correct samples (<math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{corr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>corr</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{corr}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{\text{OT}}=\frac{1}{N_{\text{corr}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{\text{corr}}}\left(1-\frac{\hat{T}_{i}}{T_{i}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mtext>OT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>corr</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>corr</mtext></msub></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{\text{OT}}=\frac{1}{N_{\text{corr}}}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{\text{corr}}}\left(1-\frac{\hat{T}_{i}}{T_{i}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total length and <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{T}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>T</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{T}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the effective length up to the onset of stagnation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Underthinking Score (<math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{\text{UT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">UT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{\text{UT}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> measures pre-solution stagnation (e.g., structural loops or lack of progress) on incorrect samples (<math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{inc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>inc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{inc}}</annotation></semantics></math>). It utilizes the identical formulation as <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{\text{OT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mtext>OT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{\text{OT}}</annotation></semantics></math> but is computed over the set of incorrect responses. For both metrics, lower scores indicate higher stability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metacognition Score</span> evaluates the richness of metacognitive integration. The judge assigns a score from 0 to 5 based on how actively the model implements key metacognitive behaviors, regardless of the answer’s correctness.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The specific judge model and the full set of prompts used for these evaluations are provided in the Appendix <a href="#A5.SS3" title="E.3 Behavioral Evaluation Prompt ‣ Appendix E Evaluation Prompts ‣ Mirroring the Mind: Distilling Human-LikeMetacognitive Strategies into Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Multi-Hop QA Reasoning Performance</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Datasets ‣ 4.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Mirroring the Mind: Distilling Human-LikeMetacognitive Strategies into Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes MHQA reasoning performance across model scales under ID and OOD settings.
We observe that prompt-based metacognitive elicitation (Base+Prompt) yields limited improvements and often degrades OOD performance, suggesting that superficial prompting alone is insufficient to induce robust metacognitive control.
Similarly, Standard GRPO substantially improves ID accuracy but exhibits inconsistent generalization to OOD benchmarks, particularly on the complex MuSiQue dataset.
Rejection Sampling (RS), which trains models using self-generated correct traces, provides modest gains but fails to ensure robust performance shifts across distributions.
Furthermore, efficiency-oriented methods such as TokenSkip and LIMOPro, while designed to optimize computational cost, often underperform on OOD benchmarks, indicating that aggressive trace compression strategies may compromise the structural stability required for complex reasoning.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, MBT consistently achieves the strongest performance across all datasets and model sizes.
Notably, its performance on MuSiQue is particularly striking, as this benchmark is substantially more challenging than the training source (HotpotQA) due to its complex evidence composition.
Despite being trained on the relatively simpler HotpotQA, MBT demonstrates higher gains on this challenging OOD task compared to the ID setting, especially for larger models like Qwen3-4B.
This result suggests that MBT does not merely fit the patterns of the training data but successfully instills a generalizable metacognitive mechanism.
Comparing the two formulations, MBT-S and MBT-R achieve comparable accuracy across most settings, suggesting that both synthesizing traces from scratch and rewriting existing traces are effective strategies for injecting robust metacognitive control.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of MBT versus naive reasoning distillation (gpt-oss-distill) on MuSiQue (Qwen3-4B). While naive distillation mimics the teacher’s accuracy, it suffers from severe inefficiency and frequent degeneration.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S4.T3.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:52.5pt;vertical-align:-23.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(10.7pt,-1.6pt) scale(1.06593633975589,1.06593633975589) ;">
<table id="S4.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">Method</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">EM<math id="S4.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">F1<math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">LLM<math id="S4.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">Degen<math id="S4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">Len<math id="S4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">AES<math id="S4.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">gpt-oss-distill</td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">53.58</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">63.02</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="S4.T3.5.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">66.57</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">285</td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">5450</td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">-2.42</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.5.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">MBT-S (Ours)</td>
<td id="S4.T3.5.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">52.34</td>
