<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

<figure id="Ax1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table A1: </span>Answer inclusion analysis on the MuSiQue dataset.
<span id="Ax1.T1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Accuracy</span> denotes the percentage of correct predictions.
<span id="Ax1.T1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Substring Match (correct)</span> indicates the proportion of correct samples in which the gold answer string explicitly appears in the reasoning trace.
<span id="Ax1.T1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Substring Match (incorrect)</span> represents the same proportion for incorrect samples.
<span id="Ax1.T1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LLM_judge (correct)</span> and <span id="Ax1.T1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LLM_judge (incorrect)</span> respectively denote the proportions of correct and incorrect samples whether the gold answer was considered at any point during the reasoning process, following the criterion used in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Mirroring the Mind: Distilling Human-LikeMetacognitive Strategies into Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</figcaption>
