<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Ablation Study: Disentangling SFT and GRPO</h3>

<figure id="A2.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T9.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A9</span>: </span><span id="A2.T9.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
Ablation study of SFT and GRPO contributions across model scales.
We compare the impact of each training stage on accuracy and stability.
<span id="A2.T9.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MBT-S</span> and <span id="A2.T9.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MBT-R</span> denote supervised fine-tuning (SFT) using reasoning traces generated by the MBT-S (synthetic) and MBT-R (rewriting) formulations, respectively.
The full MBT (SFT+GRPO), which represents our final proposed method, achieves the optimal trade-off by leveraging SFT for structural grounding and GRPO for performance refinement.
</span></figcaption>
<div id="A2.T9.7" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:128.7pt;vertical-align:-63.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-201.5pt,75.2pt) scale(0.461265674647502,0.461265674647502) ;">
